IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cr1-helpers`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), PART IV -- PRESCRIBED INTEREST RATES AND REFUNDS OF
-- OVERPAYMENT (regulations 35 and 36). Piece cr1. LAYER 1.
--
-- Regulation 36 fixes the prescribed rate of interest from the yields of Government of Canada Treasury Bills sold
-- at auction. Those yields are published by someone else and are not among the texts this encoding reads, so the
-- yields arrive as a LIST OF NUMBER, each a percentage per annum (4.37 means 4.37 per cent). The rates the
-- module returns are fractions (0.09 is 9 per cent), as everywhere in this encoding.
-- Subsection 38(7) of the Act (piece cp2) says that interest is paid or applied; regulation 35 says from when,
-- and regulation 36(2)(b) at what rate. How the interest is compounded is not in this range.

§ `Regulations, Part IV -- prescribed interest rates and refunds of overpayment (regs 35 and 36)`

§§ `Regulation 36: the quarters and the prescribed rates`

-- 36 (1) quarter means any of the periods in a year: January 1 to March 31, April 1 to June 30, July 1 to
-- September 30, October 1 to December 31.
-- src:403 | 36 (1) For the purposes of subsection (2), quarter means any of the following periods in a year:
-- src:404 | (a) the period that begins on January 1 and ends on March 31;
-- src:405 | (b) the period that begins on April 1 and ends on June 30;
-- src:406 | (c) the period that begins on July 1 and ends on September 30; and
-- src:407 | (d) the period that begins on October 1 and ends on December 31.
@ref Reg 36(1) (src:403-407)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 36(1) — the number of the quarter of a year that contains a day` day MEANS
    (FLOOR (((DATE_MONTH day) MINUS 1) DIVIDED BY 3)) PLUS 1

@ref Reg 36(1) (src:403-407)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 36(1) — the first day of the quarter that contains a day` day MEANS
    YearMonthDay (DATE_YEAR day) ((3 TIMES ((`reg 36(1) — the number of the quarter of a year that contains a day` day) MINUS 1)) PLUS 1) 1

-- 36 (2)(a)(i) ... Treasury Bills ... sold at auctions ... during the first month of the quarter preceding the
-- particular quarter. The month, for a day, is the first month of the quarter before the one the day falls in.
-- src:408 | (2) For the purposes of
-- src:409 | (a) every provision of the Act that requires interest at a prescribed rate to be paid to the Receiver General, the prescribed rate in effect during any particular quarter is the total of
-- src:410 | (i) the rate that is the simple arithmetic mean, expressed as a percentage per annum and rounded to the next higher whole percentage where the mean is not a whole percentage, of all amounts each of which is the average equivalent yield, expressed as a percentage per annum, of Government of Canada Treasury Bills that mature approximately three months after their date of issue and that are sold at auctions of Government of Canada Treasury Bills during the first month of the quarter preceding the particular quarter, and
-- src:411 | (ii) 4 per cent; and
@ref Reg 36(2)(a)(i) (src:408-411)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 36(2)(a)(i) — the first month of the quarter preceding the quarter that contains a day` day MEANS
    `add months` (`reg 36(1) — the first day of the quarter that contains a day` day) (0 MINUS 3)

-- (i) the rate that is the simple arithmetic mean, expressed as a percentage per annum and rounded to the next
-- higher whole percentage where the mean is not a whole percentage, of all the average equivalent yields of
-- Treasury Bills that mature approximately three months after issue and are sold at those auctions. NOTHING when
-- there is no yield to take a mean of.
@ref Reg 36(2)(a)(i) (src:408-411)
GIVEN yields IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 36(2)(a)(i) — the whole percentage that is the mean of the Treasury Bill yields` yields MEANS
    IF count yields EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (CEILING ((sum yields) DIVIDED BY (count yields)))

-- 36 (2)(a) the prescribed rate in effect during a quarter, for every provision of the Act that requires interest at
-- a prescribed rate to be paid to the Receiver General, is the total of that percentage and (ii) 4 per cent.
-- src:409 | (a) every provision of the Act that requires interest at a prescribed rate to be paid to the Receiver General, the prescribed rate in effect during any particular quarter is the total of
-- src:410 | (i) the rate that is the simple arithmetic mean, expressed as a percentage per annum and rounded to the next higher whole percentage where the mean is not a whole percentage, of all amounts each of which is the average equivalent yield, expressed as a percentage per annum, of Government of Canada Treasury Bills that mature approximately three months after their date of issue and that are sold at auctions of Government of Canada Treasury Bills during the first month of the quarter preceding the particular quarter, and
-- src:411 | (ii) 4 per cent; and
@ref Reg 36(2)(a) (src:409-411)
GIVEN yields IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 36(2)(a) — the prescribed rate on an amount payable to the Receiver General` yields MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 36(2)(a)(i) — the whole percentage that is the mean of the Treasury Bill yields` yields
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST percentage THEN JUST ((percentage PLUS 4) DIVIDED BY 100)

-- 36 (2)(b) the prescribed rate in effect during a quarter, for every provision of the Act that requires interest
-- at a prescribed rate to be paid or applied on an amount payable by the Minister, is the total of the rate under
-- (a)(i) and (ii) if the amount is payable to a corporation, zero per cent, and in any other case, 2 per cent.
-- src:412 | (b) every provision of the Act that requires interest at a prescribed rate to be paid or applied on an amount payable by the Minister, the prescribed rate in effect during any particular quarter is the total of
-- src:413 | (i) the rate determined under subparagraph (a)(i) in respect of the particular quarter, and
-- src:414 | (ii) if the amount is payable to a corporation, zero per cent, and in any other case, 2 per cent.
@ref Reg 36(2)(b) (src:412-414)
GIVEN yields IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the amount is payable to a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 36(2)(b) — the prescribed rate on an amount payable by the Minister` yields `the amount is payable to a corporation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 36(2)(a)(i) — the whole percentage that is the mean of the Treasury Bill yields` yields
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST percentage THEN JUST ((percentage PLUS (IF `the amount is payable to a corporation` THEN 0 ELSE 2)) DIVIDED BY 100)

§§ `Regulation 35: from when interest runs on an overpayment`

-- 35 (a) Where an amount in respect of an overpayment of contributions is refunded to an employee or a
-- self-employed person or applied to a liability of the employee or self-employed person to Her Majesty in right of
-- Canada, interest to be paid or applied under subsection 38(7) of the Act shall be calculated at the rate
-- prescribed in paragraph 36(2)(b) and for the period that begins on the latest of (i) May 1 of the year following
-- the year for which the contributions were paid, (ii) the day on which the application for the refund was received,
-- and (iii) the day on which the overpayment arose, and ends on the day on which the amount is so refunded or applied.
-- Where no application for the refund was received, (ii) names no day and the latest of the others governs.
-- src:393 | 35 Where
-- src:394 | (a) an amount in respect of an overpayment of contributions is refunded to an employee or a self-employed person or applied to a liability of the employee or self-employed person to Her Majesty in right of Canada, interest to be paid or applied under subsection 38(7) of the Act shall be calculated at the rate prescribed in paragraph 36(2)(b) and for the period that begins on the latest of
-- src:395 | (i) May 1 of the year following the year for which the contributions were paid,
-- src:396 | (ii) the day on which the application for the refund was received, and
-- src:397 | (iii) the day on which the overpayment arose,
-- src:398 | and ends on the day on which the amount is so refunded or applied; and
@ref Reg 35(a)(ii) (src:393-398)
GIVEN `the day the application for the refund was received` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the overpayment arose` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 35(a)(ii) — the day the application for the refund was received, or the day the overpayment arose where there was no application` `the day the application for the refund was received` `the day the overpayment arose` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the application for the refund was received`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day the overpayment arose`
    WHEN JUST received THEN received

@ref Reg 35(a) (src:393-398)
GIVEN `the year for which the contributions were paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the application for the refund was received` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the overpayment arose` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 35(a) — the first day of the period for which interest runs on an overpayment refunded to an employee or a self-employed person` `the year for which the contributions were paid` `the day the application for the refund was received` `the day the overpayment arose` MEANS
    `cr1 helper: the later of two dates`
        (YearMonthDay (`the year for which the contributions were paid` PLUS 1) 5 1)
        (`cr1 helper: the later of two dates`
            `the day the overpayment arose`
            (`reg 35(a)(ii) — the day the application for the refund was received, or the day the overpayment arose where there was no application` `the day the application for the refund was received` `the day the overpayment arose`))

-- 35 (b) Where an amount in respect of an overpayment is refunded to an employer or applied to a liability of the
-- employer to Her Majesty in right of Canada, interest ... at the rate prescribed in paragraph 36(2)(b) and for the
-- period that begins on the later of (i) the day on which the remittance that created the overpayment was received,
-- and (ii) the day on which that remittance was due to be received, and ends on the day on which the amount is so
-- refunded or applied.
-- src:399 | (b) an amount in respect of an overpayment is refunded to an employer or applied to a liability of the employer to Her Majesty in right of Canada, interest to be paid or applied under subsection 38(7) of the Act shall be calculated at the rate prescribed in paragraph 36(2)(b) and for the period that begins on the later of
-- src:400 | (i) the day on which the remittance that created the overpayment was received, and
-- src:401 | (ii) the day on which the remittance that created the overpayment was due to be received,
-- src:402 | and ends on the day on which the amount is so refunded or applied.
@ref Reg 35(b) (src:399-402)
GIVEN `the day the remittance that created the overpayment was received` IS A DATE
      `the day the remittance that created the overpayment was due to be received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 35(b) — the first day of the period for which interest runs on an overpayment refunded to an employer` `the day the remittance that created the overpayment was received` `the day the remittance that created the overpayment was due to be received` MEANS
    `cr1 helper: the later of two dates` `the day the remittance that created the overpayment was received` `the day the remittance that created the overpayment was due to be received`
